  "body": "## What changed\n\n3D Pocket gets the shared parameter \"Pass starts at\" (Auto / Inside / Outside) of #3316. It uses the same type, key, row and MCP door as 2D Offset.\n\n- `OpParams::Pocket3D` and the engine's `Pocket3DParams` get the field `pass_start: machining2d::PassStart`. The engine field has a doc line that keeps room for the start and exit points of #1448. There is no code for them.\n- Project file: the key `pass_start` (`PassStartDto`). The file does not write `auto`. A file without the key reads Auto. There is no version step.\n- Digest: `digest::write_pass_start` writes the value only off Auto. Each earlier operation keeps its cache stamp.\n- Planner (`crates/motion/src/machining3d/level_side.rs`, new, and `hsm.rs`): Waterline and Offset rings call the 2D ring law through the new door `machining2d::level_ring_plan` (`level_rings.rs`). The door uses the same `level_pieces`, `order` and completeness guard as 2D Offset. The 3D level's cutter-centre area is its own outline, so the start side is read off the edges of `center` (offset 0). The 2D `ring_plan` keeps its arguments and its output.\n- Auto: the same `plan_passes` call as before. No Auto move can change.\n- Zigzag, and Auto (which cuts rows): no ring order. The moves do not change. The path says `PASS_START_ZIGZAG_NOTE` once. The Adaptive HSM spiral: no ring order, `PASS_START_ADAPTIVE_NOTE` once. The rest pass: `PASS_START_REST_NOTE` once. The rotary wrap keeps Auto. Rotary Offset and Multi-Axis Rough always send Auto.\n- UI: the shared row `Pass starts at` on the 3D Pocket Passes tab. If the strategy is not Waterline or Offset rings, a line under the row says that the value is not used (`POCKET3D_NO_RING_ORDER`).\n- MCP: no new code. The generic `edit_operation` carries the key.\n- 30 motion test files and 17 app/ui test files get one line `pass_start: Default::default()` in their struct literals (no other change).\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/3361-pass-start-pocket3d.md`.\n\n## Hand trace of one level\n\nFixture of `pocket3d_pass_start` (motion): a 40 mm square pocket, a 10 mm square island in the middle, tool radius 3, Waterline, stepover 2.4, one level at Z 0. The cutter-centre band runs from the island ring (Chebyshev distance 8 from the island centre, 7.1 at the round corners) to the wall ring (17). The numbers are the Chebyshev distance of each ring, in cut order.\n\n- Auto: 12.2 -> 14.6 -> 17.0, then 12.2, then 10.4 -> 8.8, then the island ring 8.0 last. This is the core-first order of today.\n- Inside: island ring 8.0 first -> 10.4 -> 12.8 -> 15.2 -> the wall ring 17 last. The path says the island wall note.\n- Outside: the wall ring 17.0 first -> 14.6 -> 12.2 -> 9.8 -> 7.4 (clipped pieces) -> the island ring last. The path says the outer wall note.\n\nNo completeness fallback on any value. Each cut stays in the band.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion` `pocket3d_pass_start`:\n  - `inside_and_outside_force_the_ring_order_of_a_3d_level` (Waterline and Offset rings). The test was red first: with the side forced to Auto, it failed with \"Waterline: Inside starts on the island ring, at 12.2\".\n  - `zigzag_keeps_its_rows_and_names_the_unused_choice` (Zigzag and Auto: the same moves, the note once).\n- `camcraft-app` `pocket3d_pass_start`:\n  - `the_generate_arm_hands_pass_start_to_the_3d_ladder` (40 mm block in its stock, Waterline, the first cut of each value, no added verify warning).\n  - `pocket3d_pass_start_rides_the_project_file` (key absent for Auto, present for Inside and Outside, a file without the key reads Auto, an unknown word is refused).\n  - `mcp_sets_pocket3d_pass_start_and_undo_redo_walk_it` (`edit_operation`, undo, redo).\n- `camcraft-app` lib: `pass_start_moves_the_pocket3d_stamp_only_off_auto`.\n- `camcraft-ui` lib: `the_pocket3d_passes_tab_offers_pass_start_and_names_the_row_strategies`, and the 3D Pocket row of `every_field_lives_on_exactly_one_section`.\n\n## Readings (debug, -j 6, head 22ebe663b)\n\n- motion: lib 548 ok; `pocket3d_pass_start` 2; `pass_start_levels` 7; `pocket3d_hsm` 3 (1 ignored); `pocket3d_mask_edge` 6; `pocket3d_troch` 5; `machining3d` 23; `level_links` 12; `offset_shells` 6; `top_z_level` 13.\n- app: lib 299; `pocket3d_pass_start` 3; `golden_cl` 33; `conformance` 7; `project_roundtrip` 80; `operations` 121; `mcp` 26; `mcp_doc_drift` 6; `mcp_enum_patch` 3; `mcp_pockets` 3; `example_catalog` 37; `example_catalog_adaptive` 1; `example_catalog_edge_work` 1; `first_part_programs` 2; `drill_prior` 12; `level_links` 25; `pocket3d_air_band` 4; `pocket3d_hsm` 2; `pocket3d_open_side` 7; `pocket3d_reach` 6; `pocket3d_trochoid` 5 (holds the one 3D pocket golden, `pocket3d_trochoidal_pocket.cl`: no change); `remachining` 6; `rest_across_setups` 7; `setup_align_3d` 6; `suppressed_rest` 2; `tool_body_beside_shank` 5; `carried_engine_agreement` 3; `adaptive_pass_start` 4; `offset_pass_start` 4.\n- ui: lib 1486.\n- clippy `-D warnings`: motion `--all-targets`, app `--lib`, ui `--all-targets`: clean.\n- No golden file changed.\n\n## Not run\n\n- These motion binaries got only the one-line literal insert. They compile (`cargo check -p camcraft-motion --all-targets` is clean), but they did not run: `avoid_pocket`, `blind_floor`, `center_cut_law`, `engagement_3d`, `entry_arc_3d`, `equal_steps`, `multiaxis_avoid`, `multiaxis_rough`, `one_descent`, `pivot5d`, `pocket_refusal`, `pocket_wall_finish_levels`, `posed_subtract`, `radial_step`, `rotary_adaptive`, `rotary_dflat`, `rotary_links`, `rotary_offset`.\n- No heavy lane (P2). `stock_play_cost_bench` and `stock_engine_agreement` have only ignored tests.\n- The HSM planner's own fallback to rings does not read the value. Follow-up: #3616 (P7).\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill row still says that other kinds get the key in their own issues. It is a process file, so this PR does not change it.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: 3D Pocket has \"Pass starts at\" (Auto / Inside / Outside) on its Passes tab, in MCP `edit_operation` and in the project file. Inside and Outside set where the Waterline and Offset rings start on each level; Auto keeps the earlier order.\n\nRefs #3316\nRefs #1448\n\nFixes #3361\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
